=====================================================================
PART 1 — THE REMEASUREMENT SPEC (Module A's own trigger; this is the
instrument that resolves the two boundary CELLS)
=====================================================================
The lock, Section 4: a BOUNDARY-INDETERMINATE species "triggers
independent remeasurement." Module C cannot do this job (Part 2).

SPECIMENS
- Natural iridium, single crystal (or Rietveld-grade powder), terrestrial
  isotopic abundance (clause C2), no synthetic enrichment.
- Natural osmium, same form. (Handle as the metal; OsO4 safety protocol
  is the lab's standing duty — no heating in air.)
- Reference state: T = 293.15 K, P = 1 atm (clause C1). Temperature
  controlled and STATED to within +/-2 K; beyond that the species is
  TEMPERATURE-INDETERMINATE, not classified.

MEASUREMENT
- Single-crystal XRD refined cell (tier 1) or powder Rietveld (tier 2).
- rho computed ONLY as rho = Z * M / (N_A * V_cell), M at IUPAC
  terrestrial atomic weights (Ir 192.217, Os 190.23).
- Uncertainty propagated from the cell parameters to a 95% CI for rho.

PRECISION BARS (computed 2026-11-14 from the EQS-1209 determinations)
- IRIDIUM: the 1963 point estimate sits 45.3 kg/m3 (0.201%) below rho*.
  A determination decides the species if its 95% CI half-width is
  < 45 kg/m3, i.e. cell edge known to ~0.0026 A or better. Routine
  modern XRD (+/-0.0005 A) yields rho to ~ +/-9 kg/m3 — one modern
  measurement at the stated temperature DECIDES iridium, either way.
- OSMIUM: the 1998 point estimate sits 16.3 kg/m3 (0.072%) below rho*.
  Required CI half-width < 16 kg/m3: cell edges to ~ +/-0.0007 A class
  with temperature held inside the C1 window. High-grade but standard
  single-crystal work.
- Temperature leverage: volumetric expansion ~1.9e-5 /K moves rho by
  ~4.3 kg/m3 per 10 K — inside the C1 +/-2 K window it is < 1 kg/m3
  and cannot carry the verdict.

DECISION RULES (the lock's, verbatim in effect)
- 95% CI entirely inside the band  -> CONFORMING.
- 95% CI entirely above 22604.3007 -> FALSIFIED: one such species kills
  the occupancy claim as scoped (MINC3). No re-banding is permitted.
- CI still straddling              -> remains BOUNDARY-INDETERMINATE;
  the next remeasurement is specified, not improvised.

WHAT THIS COSTS IN KIND: two specimens, one diffractometer, days of
lab time — the smallest experiment in the entire minerals program,
and the only one standing between the law and a closed boundary.

=====================================================================
PART 2 — MODULE C CRITERIA (from Preregistration v1.0 Sections 5-6,
AS LOCKED — tests whether rho* is a physical state boundary; does
NOT test occupancy and cannot falsify Module A)
=====================================================================
CROSSING PATH 1 — IRIDIUM ISOTOPE SERIES (constant chemistry class)
rho(x) = 22562 * Mbar(x) / 192.216056, x = fraction of 193Ir.
Crossover at x = 0.806980 (rho = rho* exactly).
Target specimens: x = 0.75, 0.79, 0.807, 0.82, 0.85, 1.00 — each with
mass-spectrometric enrichment assay AND single-crystal XRD density.
Classification only from measured specimen density (a +/-10 kg/m3
anchor error moves the predicted crossover by ~4.3 points of x).

CROSSING PATH 2 — OSMIUM PRESSURE TRAJECTORY (isothermal 293.15 K)
Birch-Murnaghan (K0' = 4), anchor Os = 22,587 kg/m3:
K0 = 350 -> 0.268 GPa | 395 -> 0.303 | 400 -> 0.307 (nominal) |
462 -> 0.354 GPa at the crossing.

CROSSING PATH 3 — OSMIUM TEMPERATURE TRAJECTORY (isobaric 1 atm)
Cooling alone crosses at T = 238-248 K across the alpha_V range
(nominal 243.11 K at alpha_V = 15.3e-6 /K), read by cryo-XRD rho(T).

COMBINED P-T LINE (nominal): P_cross(T) = 400 * [0.000765665 +
15.3e-6 * (T - 293.15)] GPa — 0.796 GPa at 373.15 K down to 0 at
243.11 K.

A crossing COUNTS only if the measured density's 95% CI lies entirely
on the far side of rho*.

PRIMARY ENDPOINTS at each crossing: equation-of-state parameters
(K0, K0'); phonon response (Debye temperature / phonon DOS / Raman
mode frequencies). Secondary: cohesive energy per atom, electrical
resistivity. EXCLUDED as primaries: hardness, bulk conductivity.

MECHANISM SUPPORTED requires ALL of:
(a) a discontinuity, kink, or change point in >= 1 primary observable
    located at rho* within the combined density uncertainty;
(b) reproduced on >= 2 independent crossing paths;
(c) the filed boundary beats placebo boundaries at 0.95, 0.99, 1.01,
    1.05 x rho* in the pre-registered model comparison, out of sample.
MECHANISM NOT SUPPORTED: all primaries cross smoothly on all paths,
or effects track P / T / isotope mass rather than density. That
outcome leaves Module A untouched: the seat then stands as a density
coordinate, and occupancy stands or falls by Module A alone.

